Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: Aspen Discovery
Source: https://github.com/Aspen-Discovery/aspen-discovery

Comment:
 License audit status for redistribution from an apt repository. The
 stanzas below come from a full inventory of the bundled components.
 .
 Three bundled files are NOT freely redistributable and must be resolved
 before this package is served from a public repository:
 .
  * code/carlx_export/lib/ojdbc6.jar: Oracle JDBC 11.2.0.4, proprietary
    (Oracle OTN license). Remove from the package or restrict the
    repository; only CARL.X sites need it.
  * sites/default/GeoIPCity.dat: legacy MaxMind GeoIP City data with no
    license file. Legacy GeoIP data is under a restrictive MaxMind EULA
    (old GeoLite was CC-BY-SA 3.0 with attribution). Verify its origin
    or drop it.
  * code/java_shared_libraries/src/org/json/: the JSON License ("shall
    be used for Good, not Evil") is considered non-free by Debian. Only
    the source is bundled here; it is compiled into the module jars.
 .
 Also note: ua-parser.js is AGPL-3.0 (strong copyleft, fine for a
 private repository); the fonts under code/web/fonts/ ship without
 their license texts (OFL-1.1 requires the notice to accompany the
 fonts); glyphicons-halflings is only freely licensed as part of
 Bootstrap; and several (L)GPL jars are shipped as prebuilt binaries
 (mysql-connector-java, marc4j, log4j), for which a source offer must
 be documentable.

